{"id":"GRAM-PRON-018","category":"object_clitic","status":"provisional","form":"idin","person":2,"number":"plural","review_evidence":"native_speaker_project_review","reviewed_examples":["May idin cunaysaa?","Maydin cunaysaa?","Libaaxu muu idin eryanayaa?","Haa, wuu na eryanayaa."],"note":"Native project review confirms idin as the second-person plural object in these constructions. It does not control subject gender/number agreement on the verb.","source":"SLS resources/naxwe/04-sarfaha-magacuyaallada.md"}
