{"id":"GRAM-PRON-022","category":"subject_clitic_source_analysis","status":"context_required","form":"aydin","person":2,"number":"plural","review_evidence":"native_speaker_project_review","status_note":"Do not globally analyze waydin as an ordinary second-person-plural subject marker. Native review shows surface waydin/maydin can contain object idin in constructions where an understood or explicit third-person subject performs the action, e.g. Maydin cunaysaa? and Libaaxu maydin eryanayaa?. Keep the SLS source analysis for comparison, but resolve morphology by construction before execution.","source":"SLS resources/naxwe/04-sarfaha-magacuyaallada.md"}
